  "note": "Annual election of one third of the council (five seats), Monday 15 January 1900, to replace the five members elected in 1899 with the lowest votes (John A. Thompson, William White, John Mahaffy, John Dobson and John Soye). Thompson, White and Mahaffy sought re-election; Douie, McNeice and Creaney stood as working-men's (Labour) candidates. \"Of the 2,606 electors on the register only 1,024 voted. There were 12 spoiled voting papers.\" No party labels printed. John Mahaffy: no party label printed in 1900. At other elections he stood as Unionist (Lurgan, 16 January 1899, listed as Unionist: Belfast News-Letter, 18 January 1899, p. 7 (\"Urban District Councils\"); Lurgan, 15 January 1912, printed 'U.': Lurgan Mail, 20 January 1912, p. 5 (\"The Municipal Election: A Heavy Poll\"); labels from the Lurgan Times, 20 January 1912, p. 2 (\"Monday's Election\")). William White: no party label printed in 1900. At other elections he stood as Unionist (Lurgan, Armagh County Council, 28 May 1902, printed 'U': Armagh Guardian, 2 May 1902, p. 2 (\"But Few Contests\": county council nominations, with labels); members confirmed by the Lurgan Times, 7 June 1902, p. 3 (\"Armagh County Council\": complete list of the elected members))."
